{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_53","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1921,1979p' \\\"/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/curator/.task-board/.resources/TASK-260720-1nvomm/TASK-260720-1nvomm_external-build-repositories-architecture-v6.md\\\"\"","aggregated_output":"### 17.1 Producer verification evidence\n\nChecks performed on 2026-07-27:\n\n- all thirteen fenced JSON documents parsed with the host Python JSON parser;\n- targeted topic checks found the exact init/fetch vectors,\n  `GIT_SSH_VARIANT=ssh`, wrapper argv contract, `-F` SSH isolation, stable\n  gitfile/bare/linked/reftable errors, config/ref grammar, exact pack-2/3 and\n  index-2 admission, the full-OID-only batch request/response grammar, manager\n  object-ID recomputation, common commit/tag semantic grammar, pinned-family\n  all-blob LFS detector, audit-before-cache/compiler ordering, mixed\n  receipt/marker behavior, status/repair/GC, signing, future-driver rules, and\n  board-impact mapping;\n- the new Git fetch/init/repository-version/reftable/layout/config and OpenSSH\n  manual pages in section 16 were opened from their primary maintainers and\n  checked against the claims above;\n- a temporary local-transport smoke on Git 2.50.1 exercised the exact\n  init/common-fetch option shape for both full-object and exact-tag refspecs,\n  verified the fixed `refs/curator/*` destinations, and verified that\n  `FETCH_HEAD` was absent;\n- a revision-6 Git 2.50.1 smoke repeated exact-tag-only acquisition with\n  `uploadpack.allowAnySHA1InWant` disabled and enabled: matching annotated tags\n  fetched and peeled to the lock, moved lightweight tags fetched but failed the\n  manager equality check, missing tags made fetch exit 128, no direct object-ID\n  refspec was attempted, and `FETCH_HEAD` remained absent in all six cases;\n- a task-local Git 2.50.1 raw-object smoke used the exact `cat-file --batch`\n  argv against SHA-1 and SHA-256 private repositories; full-ID requests\n  returned the documented `<oid> <type> <size> LF`, exact content bytes, and\n  terminal LF, while no filter/textconv/mailmap option or child process was\n  used;\n- Git LFS 3.7.1 source and binary checks confirmed the `<1024` cutoff,\n  `bytes.TrimSpace`/ScanLines behavior, current/alias versions, one-digit\n  prefix-only extension regexp, exact-key overwrite, distinct-priority\n  rejection, signed-int64 size parsing, and empty encoding for size zero;\n- the checked official `v3.7.1/lfs/pointer.go` bytes hashed to\n  `sha256:3aa4a0df7ed9b3c8f45742a4e01909feeb721017bfbd70e2a166132b2a814b2d`;\n  the local binaries were Git 2.50.1 and Git LFS 3.7.1;\n- pinned Git LFS 3.7.1 strict checks returned zero for the canonical lowercase,\n  dot/dash, underscore, uppercase, and punctuation-suffix extension fixture,\n  and returned two for the deliberately noncanonical non-empty size-zero\n  fixture;\n- independent cross-language fixture checks covered the exact 1023/1024 cutoff,\n  CRLF/blank/unsorted/no-final-LF forms, exact duplicate keys, distinct\n  duplicate priorities, non-empty size zero, punctuation-start and uppercase-\n  OID near misses;\n- Git 2.50.1 raw-object smoke and the manager grammar fixtures covered valid\n  signed/extra-header commits and tags, duplicate/misordered tree/object/type\n  headers, malformed separators, declared/actual target mismatch, and identical\n  network-private/local-inert expected results;\n- unchanged curator-spec validation passed:\n  `validated 30 schemas and 93 vector files`;\n- the pinned validation environment's full `make validate` passed all 30\n  schemas, 93 vectors, 8 Python tests, and `go test ./tools/...`;\n- the official Git fetch and upload-pack configuration documentation was\n  rechecked for explicit tag refspecs, `--no-tags`, empty refmap,\n  `--no-write-fetch-head`, and direct-object want policy;\n- `git diff --check` passed in curator-spec;\n- this run did not edit product/spec/schema/code/test/release files or any\n  prior producer/reviewer resource.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
